    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0594" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1735: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-02T17:00:00-05:00">March 2, 1940—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 78 and 79. We have taken up the matter as vigorously as possible with
                    White and separately with Traphagen<anchor n="15" xml:id="d675-f1"/> of the
                    Council. It will be considered at a special meeting of the Executive Committee
                    on Monday morning and we will telegraph you as soon as possible thereafter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d675-f1" n="15" xml:id="d675-f1-content">
                <p>John C. Traphagen.</p>
            </note>
